        "original_id": "9cc8383e-c583-55a1-b038-520d3795c799",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Markus Feehily, Bobby Fuller\n- Music Groups: The Bobby Fuller Four, Westlife\n- Works: Fire, \"Love's Made a Fool of You\", \"I Fought the Law\"\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, guitarist, vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Bobby Fuller was born on October 22, 1942, and was an American rock singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Bobby Fuller was best known for \"Love's Made a Fool of You\" and for his cover of \"I Fought the Law\" recorded with his mid-1960s group The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Bobby Fuller died on July 18, 1966.\n- Markus Feehily was born on 28 May 1980 and was formerly known as Mark Feehily.\n- Markus Feehily is an Irish singer and songwriter.\n- Fire is the debut solo studio album by Markus Feehily, who was also a vocalist in Westlife.",
